2A AGENCY: AI-IQ PROTOCOL v1.0

1. OBJECTIVE
This protocol establishes the official framework for measuring and notarizing Algorithmic Integrity and Brand Identity Stability ("AI-IQ") for global entities. It serves as a decentralized System of Record on Base L2.

2. VALIDATION STANDARD
All audits issued by 2A Agency (Validator: 0x8269781b855d2987e9873ff1a3a81878e77665b1) comply with the ERC-8004 Trust Framework, ensuring the Identity, Reputation, and Validation of monitored brands.

3. METHODOLOGY
The AI-IQ Score (0-100) is calculated based on three pillars:

Data Sovereignty: Protection against customer data drift.

Model Transparency: Auditability of autonomous systems.

Identity Integrity: Resistance of brand DNA to algorithmic degradation.

4. IMMUTABILITY
Each audit is hashed using the Keccak-256 algorithm and anchored on Base Mainnet. Any modification to the score or the audit date invalidates the cryptographic proof.

5. REGISTRY AUTHORITY
As of March 2026, this protocol governs the 500+ certification records issued by 2A Agency, establishing the primary benchmark for AI Brand Authority on the Base Ecosystem.